WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:13.000
Hey Team it’s Charlie and as requested this
video is going to be a history of the Constantine

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:25.539
character in the comics along with an explanation
of what’s going on with the show.

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:30.740
I have seen the first episode so I’ll probably
just post a non-spoilery review next week.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:40.489
But yes, it was a lot of fun.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:42.870
Hello any new people, if you’re just finding
me for the first time.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.340
I’ll be doing Constantine videos every friday
night this season, be sure to subscribe to

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.730
join the team.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.609
We have a good time.

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:55.499
I’m going to start with the story of how
the character was created and then I’ll

00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:58.769
do his fictional biography inside the canon.

00:00:58.769 --> 00:01:02.909
The New 52 reboot changed a few aspects of
his backstory, so I’ll try to incorporate

00:01:02.909 --> 00:01:05.610
some of those as I go along.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:11.380
In real life, the character John Constantine
was created by Alan Moore inside the Swamp

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.579
Thing comics in 1985, he was introduced as
Swamp Thing’s Supernatural Advisor.

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:21.250
The design of the character was actually based
on Sting, the musician.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.671
The reason he looks like Sting is because
the artists on the Swamp Thing comic were

00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:30.270
huge Police fans and wanted to draw a character
that looked like Sting.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.340
So Alan Moore invented John Constantine.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.140
The funny thing about that is that the first
artist to actually draw the Constantine character

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.140
was a totally different person.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.580
Rick Veitch drew his debut in Swamp Thing
number 37.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:41.649
There were all kinds of real life occult things
that Alan Moore threw into the character like

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:46.159
serial killers, the Winchester House, which
is an actual place all piled into Sting’s

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:47.159
appearance.

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:52.729
He did this interview at 1985 San Diego Comic
Con where he explained that Constantine was

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:59.280
turning into something much bigger than a
simple ‘put our favorite musician into a

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.280
story’ character.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.749
At his core he’s a character that always
has an answer for everything, has many agents

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:12.050
working for him all at once, seemingly knows
everyone and is constantly manipulating people.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:17.160
DC was originally very worried that Sting
would sue them for making a character that

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.520
looked like him but Sting himself was really
happy about it.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.700
In 1988 the character got his own title, Hellblazer.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.910
Which is what inspired the tv series.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:31.460
Then in 2011 he was also made a part of the
Justice League Dark team, so he appears in

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.170
that title and the Hellblazer comic since
the new 52 reboot.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:42.130
Justice League Dark for those that don’t
know is just a Justice League made up of all

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:48.060
the supernatural characters like Zatanna,
Madame Xanadu, Deadman and Frankenstein.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.820
Here’s his fictional character biography.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.950
A lot of this wasn’t written into the canon
until the Hellblazer comic started.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:03:00.210
Way after Alan Moore stopped writing the character.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:05.130
He was born in Liverpool in 1953, because
of complications from an earlier abortion.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.420
His mother died giving birth to him and his
twin brother.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:16.050
Supposedly his twin was killed in the womb
after John’s umbilical cord strangled him.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:24.140
His father, who had forced the mother to get
an abortion couldn’t handle her death and

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.140
blamed John.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.900
Thus they developed an unhealthy father son
relationship from the start.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.320
You can already see, he’s got the origins
of a crazy person.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:42.320
His family bloodline descended from the Laughing
Mages, a group of mages who had the ability

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.740
to trick gods.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.680
Eventually John learned about this and it
inspired him to take up magic.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.950
One of his first acts of magic was to distill
all of his childhood innocence into a physical

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.620
box as a literal way to get rid of it.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:07.230
He ran away from home and started living with
Francis Chandler also called Chas, he’s

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.730
being played by Charles Halford in the TV
Series.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.670
You’ll see him in the first episode.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.660
Chas became his best and longest surviving
friend.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:28.560
Then John got involved with all the big occult
circles in London and eventually started dating

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.260
Zatarra.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:44.510
Started a band named Mucous Membrane and even
released an album called Venus of the Hardsell.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:52.380
Eventually he decided to play the hero, but
his first act of good was a disaster.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.920
He finds a little girl in the aftermath of
a magical orgy gone horribly wrong.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:01.030
The little girl had raised a demon to punish
everyone for what they’d done to her and

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:06.740
to try and banish the demon, John raised a
demon of his own.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.730
But he wasn’t able to control it.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:15.410
So John’s demon killed the other demon and
his friends and took the child to hell.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.670
After which John suffered a mental breakdown
and was committed to Ravenscar Psychiatric

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.670
Hospital.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.130
He was in and out of that place for years.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:25.880
In the first episode we learn all about the
little girl, since the comics have already

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.880
closed that saga I’m just going to skip
what happens to avoid spoilers.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:28.880
But you can imagine.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.230
Before the new 52 reboot he would go on to
be involved in several magical wars and big

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.580
occult stories in the UK.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:51.510
The big difference between the 
character in the Hellblazer comics and the

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:55.200
one in Justice League Dark, they’re two
different characters, is that the DC Version

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.360
is young and the older Hellblazer version
is in his 60s.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:06.580
DC Comics explained it this way, the Constantine
of the Hellblazer stories has aged in real

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.810
time since his debut.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:14.770
So for every year of the comic, he aged 1
year.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.650
In Justice League Dark, he’s a young man.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.710
On the TV Series, they don’t really get
into the Justice League Dark stories, but

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.950
the do make the character young.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:28.100
So if you want to read big stories of his
that inspired the TV Series, a couple suggestions

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:33.330
are Dangerous Habits, it introduces the idea
of Constantine having terminal lung cancer.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:44.100
The movie dealt with this, but the tv show
isn’t really doing it.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:50.000
Haunted, which is all about a battle with
an evil magician named Joshua Wright who starts

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.470
going after John’s ex girlfriends.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:07:01.400
Hard Time, this is Constantine trying to survive
in a maximum security prison.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.480
He has to rely on a lot of his tricksterish
ways to get by.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:10.970
and for some deep cuts there’s Neil Gaiman’s
run Hold Me.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.520
It’s from his early early comic book writing
days.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:22.140
It incorporates a lot of folklore that Gaiman
has become really famous for.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:26.840
As a character he does have extensive magical
training, he can even use magic to time travel.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.650
He also has this special ability called synchronicity
wave traveling.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:35.780
It gives him the supernatural ability to make
his own luck.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:40.470
Like if you were playing a board game and
your character had a luck modifier giving

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:42.900
you a bonus to your dice rolls.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.840
Constantine can manipulate his own modifier.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.010
He can give himself more luck.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:54.220
Qhe prefers not to use magical spells unless
he’s in a big battle.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:58.010
Usually he relies on quit wit to get himself
out of situations.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:04.290
In the canon, it’s rumored that he’s even
been able to trick God and Lucifer as well

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:10.240
as Superman and Batman.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.240
After the new 52 reboot when he joined Justice
League Dark, he was retconned and given some

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.590
more powerful attack based magic.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:22.310
He also has demon blood running through his
veins, first because of a transfusion from

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.919
one of his biggest demon enemies.

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:31.310
And then later sex with a succubus.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.110
The demon blood causes him to age very slowly,
and gives him regenerative abilities.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.750
Kind of like Wolverine’s healing factor.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:39.949
I’m going to do a review of the pilot next
week but there have been some big changes

00:08:39.949 --> 00:08:42.159
they’ve made to the show since they shot
that.

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:43.442
They’re still airing the pilot.

00:08:43.442 --> 00:08:46.399
That will be the first episode on Friday October
24th, so mark your calendar.

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:48.149
But here’s the changes.

00:08:48.149 --> 00:08:52.880
They re-shot a scene at the end, the big battle
they teased in the trailers.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.990
I’ll explain that during a spoiler section
of my review.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.800
They also replaced the main actress.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.879
In the pilot you guys will see, the female
lead is named Liv.

00:09:01.879 --> 00:09:05.999
She’s not a character from the comics, she’s
someone they created for the show.

00:09:05.999 --> 00:09:08.089
She’s played by Lucy Griffiths.

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:12.130
You might know her as Lady Marian from the
BBCs Robin Hood and True Blood.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:22.320
The said they just felt like the character
didn’t work the way they wanted.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.230
So they replaced her in the second episode
with the Zed character from the comics.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.490
She’s being played by Angelica Celaya.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.769
She’ll appear in the second episode.

00:09:30.769 --> 00:09:35.029
It sounds a little weird, but it’s totally
normal for a show to recast roles and make

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:37.589
changes between the pilot and the regular
episodes.

00:09:37.589 --> 00:09:41.350
I’ll talk about all the other characters
on the show when I do my review video.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.459
But they just cast the Spectre.

00:09:43.459 --> 00:09:48.190
They basically have free reign of the supernatural
corner of the DC Universe.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:52.490
So they will be bringing on a ton of comic
book characters during the season.

